tegration with Data Science Pipelines. It is packaged as a Python library with no HTTP server or Kubernetes deployment manifests of its own. [source: pyproject.toml:6-7, 30-44, ai4rag/components/utils/maas_client.py:30-62, ai4rag/utils/event_handler/event_handler.py:47-55, ai4rag/core/hpo/gam_opt.py:1]\n20:ai4rag is structured as a layered Python library organized around a RAG pipeline lifecycle: data ingestion, chunking, embedding, vector store management, retrieval, LLM generation, and evaluation. The optimization layer wraps this pipeline in a hyperparameter search driven by a GAM-based optimizer that explores combinations of chunking strategies (Docling hierarchical, LangChain recursive), embedding models, foundation models, and retrieval parameters to produce ranked RAG pattern configurations. [source: ai4rag/components/optimization/rag_templates_optimization.py:1-46, ai4rag/core/hpo/gam_opt.py:1]\n24:The vector store layer supports three pluggable backends — Milvus (with gRPC TLS and PEM certificate materialization), PGVector (PostgreSQL with connection pooling), and Chroma (ephemeral, persistent, or client/server modes) — all configured via environment variables. Credentials for S3 storage, vector stores, and the MaaS endpoint are injected through environment variables, with no Kubernetes Secret manifests defined by the component itself. [source: ai4rag/rag/vector_store/config.py:1-258, ai4rag/components/utils/s3.py:10-31]\n94:| pgvector | ~=0.5.0 | Yes | Unknown | Python package dependency |\n100:| pymilvus | ~=3.0.1 | Yes | Unknown | Python package dependency |\n149:| MILVUS_TOKEN | environment variable | Python application | runtime environment | Unknown |\n150:| PGVECTOR_PASSWORD | environment variable | Python application | runtime environment | Unknown |\n180:| **Crypto libraries** | httpx (TLS via system OpenSSL), boto3 (AWS SDK TLS), psycopg (libpq TLS), pymilvus (gRPC TLS) | pyproject.toml:31-44 |\n181:| **Certificate handling** | System trust store 