ecision record exists that names the selected provisioning approach for\n  RHOAI 3.5, with explicit go/no-go criteria, the decision date, and the\n  RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery-status evidence used.\n- The decision record names the fallback approach if the selected one fails\n  late (bring-your-own PostgreSQL or BFF-managed provisioning, as applicable).\n- The decision is recorded and socialized with the Gen AI Studio team before\n  the sprint in which the provisioning implementation starts.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box): determines the delivery\n  vehicle for the out-of-the-box experience.\n- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping): the decision confirms per-namespace scoping as\n  the model for the default vector store.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":75505,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f6d9d1b68efa09c","agent_id":"af2e6cfa74e0be569","session_id":"6460c734-9da5-4d64-9956-6c822c41e6b0","uuid":"0dfa9bc0-c586-49ce-946f-9c7b3a4c6a1f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:12:11.209Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
