vided shared PostgreSQL\n  instead of a self-provisioned instance.\n- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included) — no custom\n  image build.\n- Set resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator\n  PostgreSQL reference values, adjusted per the benchmark findings.\n- Validate end-to-end playground RAG workflows with the BFF-provisioned default\n  vector store (with the pgvector provider integration and the\n  backend-for-frontend provider wiring in place).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Configuring a playground with RAG in a namespace where no suitable PostgreSQL\n  instance exists results in the backend-for-frontend creating the\n  PostgreSQL/pgvector Deployment, Service, persistent storage, and credentials\n  secret, with no manual user setup of external infrastructure.\n- Deleting the playground cleans up the backend-provisioned PostgreSQL\n  resources.\n- Handling for pod restarts and credential rotation without a reconciliation\n  loop is designed, documented, and implemented.\n- The connection-consumption path is portable: the backend can consume a\n  platform-provided shared connection string instead of self-provisioning when\n  one becomes available.\n- End-to-end Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function out-of-the-box with\n  the BFF-provisioned default vector store, with no loss of current capability.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning).\n- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability).\n- AC-4 (vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX\n  instance).\n- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping — per-namespace isolation).\n- AC-6 (lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78246,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f6d9d1b68efa09c","agent_id":"a