{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e412fdd1-57c9-43b2-897f-b1a04143e3f2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fe00a18d9d410d0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-v496wm9z/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E005.md","content":"# Bring-your-own PostgreSQL support for Gen AI Studio playground RAG\n\n## Description\n\nImplements the bring-your-own fallback for the default vector store: customers\nprovide their own PostgreSQL (with pgvector) by configuring the OGXServer custom\nresource spec with their PostgreSQL connection details, and the playground\nconsumes that instance for RAG. This aligns with the breaking changes introduced\nin OGX 1.0 and accepts a degraded out-of-the-box experience as the recorded\nfallback: RAG capabilities in the Playground require user-provided PostgreSQL\nunder this approach. Users with production-scale vector workloads use an\nexternal vector database in any case. This branch executes if the provisioning\ngo/no-go decision selects the bring-your-own fallback (neither operator-managed\nnor BFF-managed provisioning is viable for the target release).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Validate the OGXServer custom resource connection-configuration path for\n  user-provided PostgreSQL: secret-backed connection details consumed by the\n  pgvector vector_io provider.\n- Verify the playground RAG workflow functions end-to-end with a user-provided\n  pgvector instance (with the pgvector provider integration and the\n  backend-for-frontend provider wiring in place).\n- Document the required customer configuration steps for bringing their own\n  PostgreSQL (incidental reference documentation falling out of this change —\n  no separate content work).\n- Record and communicate the out-of-the-box degradation: no silent failures\n  when RAG is used without a configured database.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user-configured OGXServer custom resource with PostgreSQL connection\n  details (secret-backed) results in playground RAG workflows functioning\n  against the user-provided pgvector instance.\n- The required configuration steps for bringing their own PostgreSQL are\n  documented for customers.\n- Behavior when RAG is invoked without a configured database is explicit and\n  communicated (clear error/guidance, no silent failure).\n- The trade-off is recorded in the go/no-go decision record: this approach does\n  not satisfy the out-of-the-box requirement and is accepted as fallback only.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the vector store, no loss of\n  current capability for users who provide a database).\n- AC-4 (vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX\n  instance).\n- AC-1 (out-of-the-box availability) is explicitly NOT satisfied under this\n  fallback — recorded in the decision record and the decomposition summary.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78246,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f6d9d1b68efa09c","agent_id":"af2e6cfa74e0be569","session_id":"6460c734-9da5-4d64-9956-6c822c41e6b0","uuid":"727804eb-38e6-412d-8877-e0f323ba6f0e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:12:50.680Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
