{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1fe8b0e8cdd7e2c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n3\ttitle: Provisioning approach go/no-go for the RHOAI 3.5 default vector store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Provisioning approach go/no-go for the RHOAI 3.5 default vector store\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves which PostgreSQL provisioning approach ships the default vector store\n30\tfor Gen AI Studio playground RAG in RHOAI 3.5. Three bounded outcomes:\n31\toperator-managed provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator\n32\tlayer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164);\n33\tBFF-managed self-provisioning by the gen-ai backend-for-frontend; or requiring\n34\tcustomers to bring their own PostgreSQL. Operator-managed provisioning has a\n35\thard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164, whose delivery timing is uncertain — this\n36\tepic runs the go/no-go gate that the development team is to define as part of\n37\tsprint planning, and records the decision that selects which provisioning\n38\timplementation proceeds.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define the go/no-go criteria and decision date for the provisioning approach\n43\t  (based on RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery status for the target release).\n44\t- Assess the delivery status of the dashboard operator modularization\n45\t  (RHAISTRAT-7164) against those criteria.\n46\t- Evaluate the BFF-managed provisioning alternative (including its lifecycle\n47\t  risks: no reconciliation loop, cleanup on playground deletion, pod restarts,\n48\t  credential rotation) against the bring-your-own PostgreSQL fallback.\n49\t- Record the decision (decision record / ADR) naming the selected approach, the\n50\t  evidence used, and the fallback if the selected approach fails late.\n51\t- Communicate the decision to the Gen AI Studio team and point the downstream\n52\t  plan at the selected implementation path.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A decision record exists that names the selected provisioning approach for\n57\t  RHOAI 3.5, with explicit go/no-go criteria, the decision date, and the\n58\t  RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery-status evidence used.\n59\t- The decision record names the fallback approach if the selected one fails\n60\t  late (bring-your-own PostgreSQL or BFF-managed provisioning, as applicable).\n61\t- The decision is recorded and socialized with the Gen AI Studio team before\n62\t  the sprint in which the provisioning implementation starts.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box): determines the delivery\n67\t  vehicle for the out-of-the-box experience.\n68\t- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping): the decision confirms per-namespace scoping as\n69\t  the model for the default vector store.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84165dc2c6681480","agent_id":"a64440399190e4b93","session_id":"6460c734-9da5-4d64-9956-6c822c41e6b0","uuid":"65144eff-ec01-471b-a925-44a56d9167d6","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:15:06.191Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1fe8b0e8cdd7e2c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
