{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdd496e1ff026893","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: Wire Gen AI Studio playground RAG to the pgvector vector_io provider\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 8\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Wire Gen AI Studio playground RAG to the pgvector vector_io provider\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThe gen-ai backend-for-frontend configures OGXServer instances for the\n35\tplayground so that RAG workflows use the remote pgvector vector_io provider,\n36\tconsuming connection details from a Kubernetes secret reference regardless of\n37\twho provisioned the database (platform operator, backend self-provisioning, or\n38\tuser-supplied configuration). This keeps the wiring independent of the\n39\tprovisioning decision and reusable when a platform-provided shared PostgreSQL\n40\tbecomes available in a later release. Application storage configuration is\n41\tunchanged.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Extend the gen-ai backend-for-frontend's OGXServer instance creation to set\n46\t  the remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration (provider activation\n47\t  setting and connection secret reference) when playground RAG is enabled.\n48\t- Keep the existing application-storage settings emitted for OGXServer\n49\t  instances unchanged (existing SQLite default).\n50\t- Use standard OGX vector_io provider settings so the connection can later be\n51\t  redirected to an externally managed vector database without backend changes\n52\t  (migration path to production-grade vector databases).\n53\t- Validate the end-to-end playground RAG workflow (document ingestion,\n54\t  embedding, retrieval) against a pgvector-backed OGX instance.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- OGXServer instances created for playgrounds with RAG enabled carry the remote\n59\t  pgvector vector_io provider configuration referencing a connection secret.\n60\t- The end-to-end playground RAG workflow (document ingestion, embedding,\n61\t  retrieval) functions against a pgvector-backed OGX instance with no manual\n62\t  vector-store setup steps in the user flow.\n63\t- Application-storage settings emitted by the backend-for-frontend are\n64\t  unchanged from current behavior.\n65\t- The provider configuration uses standard OGX vector_io settings, so the\n66\t  connection can be redirected to an external vector database without\n67\t  backend-for-frontend code changes.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning\n72\t  or configuration of external infrastructure).\n73\t- AC-2 (Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector\n74\t  store, no loss of current capability).\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84165dc2c6681480","agent_id":"a64440399190e4b93","session_id":"6460c734-9da5-4d64-9956-6c822c41e6b0","uuid":"f6e10040-25a9-4f83-8a11-969bf16a326d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:15:07.388Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdd496e1ff026893","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
