{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab402b5086275785","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E004\n3\ttitle: Benchmark pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline and finalize default\n4\t  resource sizing\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 6\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Benchmark pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline and finalize default resource sizing\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tProduces the sprint-1 benchmark and sizing deliverable for the default vector\n36\tstore: captures the inline Milvus baseline for representative playground RAG\n37\tvector operations, verifies that pgvector performs in the same order of\n38\tmagnitude (dev-experimentation scope — no latency SLA thresholds), and\n39\tfinalizes PostgreSQL resource requests/limits for the default instance,\n40\tstarting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference values. The\n41\tdefault pgvector instance targets development experimentation; users with\n42\tproduction-scale vector workloads are directed to an external vector database.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Build a benchmark harness/runbook covering representative playground RAG\n47\t  vector operations (embedding insert and similarity query) at typical\n48\t  playground document-set sizes.\n49\t- Capture the inline Milvus baseline for those operations (before inline\n50\t  providers are removed from the distribution).\n51\t- Run the same operations against the pgvector provider with the default flat\n52\t  scan (no index) configuration and compare orders of magnitude.\n53\t- Document a resource sizing recommendation for the default PostgreSQL/pgvector\n54\t  instance, starting from the model-registry-operator PostgreSQL\n55\t  requests/limits, and state whether flat scan remains adequate for typical\n56\t  playground document sets.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A benchmark report captures the inline Milvus baseline for the representative\n61\t  playground RAG vector operations.\n62\t- The pgvector results (flat scan, no index) are within the same order of\n63\t  magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline for those operations.\n64\t- A resource sizing recommendation for the default PostgreSQL/pgvector instance\n65\t  is documented, starting from the model-registry-operator PostgreSQL\n66\t  requests/limits.\n67\t- The report states whether flat scan (no index) remains adequate for typical\n68\t  playground document-set sizes, with a recommendation if adjustment is needed.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- AC-6 (default vector store lightweight enough for resource-constrained\n73\t  environments without significant overhead).\n74\t- AC-2 (no loss of current capability — measured as order-of-magnitude parity\n75\t  with the inline Milvus baseline per Staff Engineer Input).\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84165dc2c6681480","agent_id":"a64440399190e4b93","session_id":"6460c734-9da5-4d64-9956-6c822c41e6b0","uuid":"e24c63ba-3f4d-46ea-ba3a-09d8d97db7b5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:15:07.923Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab402b5086275785","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
