{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89560bdc887ff731","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E005\n3\ttitle: Operator-managed PostgreSQL provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector\n4\t  store\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) does\n17\t    not land in time for the target release, operator-managed provisioning is not\n18\t    feasible; fall back to BFF-managed provisioning or the bring-your-own PostgreSQL\n19\t    path selected by the go/no-go decision.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 0\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 4\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Operator-managed PostgreSQL provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tImplements operator-managed provisioning of the default vector store: the\n41\tRHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer (delivered by the dashboard\n42\toperator modularization, RHAISTRAT-7164) manages the full PostgreSQL/pgvector\n43\tlifecycle per namespace, following the model-registry-operator\n44\tauto-provisioning pattern. Uses the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image, which\n45\tincludes pgvector out of the box — no custom image build and no pipeline\n46\tonboarding. This branch executes if the provisioning go/no-go decision selects\n47\toperator-managed provisioning (the dashboard operator modularization lands in\n48\ttime for the target release).\n49\t\n50\t## Scope\n51\t\n52\t- Implement per-namespace PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled\n53\t  Gen AI Studio operator layer, following the model-registry-operator pattern:\n54\t  Deployment, Service, credentials secret, and storage, owned and reconciled by\n55\t  the operator.\n56\t- Generate and manage database credentials; clean up the provisioned instance on\n57\t  deletion of the owning resource.\n58\t- Set resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator\n59\t  PostgreSQL reference values, adjusted per the benchmark findings.\n60\t- Reference the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included) through\n61\t  the related-image environment variable pattern so disconnected installs work.\n62\t- Validate end-to-end playground RAG workflows with the operator-provisioned\n63\t  default vector store (with the pgvector provider integration and the\n64\t  backend-for-frontend provider wiring in place).\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- Creating or configuring a playground with RAG in a namespace results in a\n69\t  PostgreSQL/pgvector instance provisioned and managed by the operator, with no\n70\t  manual user setup of external infrastructure.\n71\t- Provisioning uses the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included)\n72\t  via the related-image reference pattern — no custom image build is introduced.\n73\t- Resource requests/limits for the provisioned instance start from the\n74\t  model-registry-operator reference values, adjusted per the benchmark findings\n75\t  when available.\n76\t- Deleting the owning resource cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL instance and\n77\t  its credentials.\n78\t- End-to-end Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function out-of-the-box with\n79\t  the operator-provisioned default vector store, with no loss of current\n80\t  capability.\n81\t\n82\t## HLR Traceability\n83\t\n84\t- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning).\n85\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability).\n86\t- AC-4 (vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX\n87\t  instance).\n88\t- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping — per-namespace isolation).\n89\t- AC-6 (lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments).\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2ed1ec0fa4412f6","agent_id":"a9bbd166cfcb65607","session_id":"6460c734-9da5-4d64-9956-6c822c41e6b0","uuid":"373115bc-433b-46b1-ac9d-fae1daead314","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:19:38.246Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89560bdc887ff731","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
