{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad7be188bd92a491","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-8004\n3\tscore: 12\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: major\n8\t  criterion: Acceptance Criteria Quality\n9\t  description: 'E003 is the replacing implementation epic (rewires playground RAG\n10\t    from the inline Milvus provider to the remote pgvector provider) but lacks the\n11\t    Rule 23 rollback/feature-flag acceptance criterion: no AC on E003 (or E002) verifies\n12\t    that disabling/reverting the pgvector provider wiring restores previous provider\n13\t    behavior. Add an AC gating on E002''s env-guarded provider activation path (e.g.,\n14\t    with the pgvector provider configuration unset/reverted, playground RAG falls\n15\t    back to the previous provider behavior during the transition before RHAISTRAT-7474\n16\t    removes inline providers).'\n17\terror: null\n18\t---\n19\t## Review Summary\n20\t\n21\tScore: 12/14 — fail\n22\tRecommendation: revise\n23\t\n24\tContract validator: OK (exit 0 — epic body sections, canonical component names, Rule 11\n25\tdocs-last coverage, priority inheritance, and Rules 7/8/10 implementation-type parallelism\n26\tall pass). Triage consistency: `triage` is null (full decomposition); multi-epic output is\n27\texpected and not penalized. One major issue found (Criterion 6), which forces that\n28\tcriterion to 0 and triggers the auto-fail rule.\n29\t\n30\t## Criterion Details\n31\t\n32\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n33\tThe strategy's HLR table was unavailable (full strategy attachment missing — documented\n34\tas Health Warning 1); the decomposition synthesized requirement IDs AC-1..AC-6 from the\n35\tstrategy's Acceptance Criteria bullets and built a traceability matrix. Every derived P0\n36\trequirement maps to at least one epic: AC-1 → E003 + BRANCH-A/B-E005 (BRANCH-C's\n37\tnon-satisfaction of the out-of-the-box clause is explicitly recorded — Health Warning 5,\n38\tthe E001 decision-record AC, and the branch-C epic body), AC-2 → E002/E003/branches,\n39\tAC-4 → E002/branches, AC-5 → branches. AC-6 (P1) maps to E004 + branches. AC-3 (Auto\n40\tRag) is explicitly deferred with justification (Staff Engineer Input override O-3:\n41\tRHOAI 3.6 / RHAISTRAT-7824; Health Warning 3 flags the stakeholder-communication need).\n42\tPriority inheritance is correct: E004 (P1) blocks no P0 work (nothing depends on it);\n43\tthe P0 branch epics are gated by P0 E001. No priority collapse: no epic bundles\n44\tdeferrable lower-priority features with P0 work. E004's HLR Traceability lists AC-2 (P0)\n45\tin addition to AC-6 (P1) — consistent with the summary matrix, whose AC-2 row records\n46\t\"validated by E004\" as the order-of-magnitude parity measurement (the P0 coverage itself\n47\tlives in E002/E003/branches), so the bundling analysis is on the record where the\n48\tmapping is read.\n49\t\n50\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n51\tNo circular dependencies. Diagram (dependency → dependent) matches epic frontmatter\n52\t`dependencies` exactly: E001 → BRANCH-A/B/C-E005, E002 → E003, E002 → E004; E001 and\n53\tE002 are roots. All three branch files set both `branch` (A/B/C, matching filenames) and\n54\t`gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001`, and `gated_by` appears in each branch's direct\n55\t`dependencies` — pipeline-droppable shape avoided. No main-plan epic lists a branch epic\n56\tin its `dependencies`. Edges are justified: E001 → branches is a true Rule 3 gate\n57\t(`remove`, three bounded outcomes → conditional branches, correct); E002 → E003 is Rule\n58\t13 (BFF wiring builds against the provider configuration surface E002 enables and\n59\tvalidates); E002 → E004 (benchmark needs a working provider). The branch epics'\n60\tintegration readiness on E002/E003 is expressed as end-to-end acceptance criteria\n61\trather than DAG edges — the sanctioned shape (branch dependencies carry the gating\n62\tInvestigation; coupling-as-AC matches the Rules 10/13 pattern), so no missing-edge\n63\tfinding. E001 ∥ E002 correctly avoids serializing Tier 1 provider work on the\n64\tRHAISTRAT-7164 timing risk. Critical path length 2 fits the strategy size heuristic.\n65\tNo konflux/license/repo epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 are vacuously satisfied.\n66\t\n67\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n68\tAll epics are single-team (Gen AI Studio); E002 is correctly separated on the component\n69\taxis (OGX Core vs Gen AI Studio). No epic spans multiple components or teams. No epic is\n70\toversized — each is a focused logical change well under the ~2-week guideline; E003's\n71\tsingle-pass-over-one-surface shape already records a concrete re-split trigger (Health\n72\tWarning 6: re-split if per-branch wiring divergence forces branch-specific code paths),\n73\twhich is a managed watch item, not a defect. No scope duplication across siblings: the\n74\tthree branch epics are mutually exclusive alternatives selected by E001, not concurrent\n75\tbuilders of the same surface; E003 (provider wiring, provenance-agnostic) and BRANCH-B\n76\t(provisioning resources) touch the same BFF but different surfaces. BRANCH-C's\n77\tcustomer-configuration documentation item is incidental reference documentation folded\n78\tinto the code change per the Rule 2 exception — not work-product type mixing.\n79\t\n80\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n81\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its go/no-go outcome determines which of three branch\n82\tepics exists (true gate, `remove`), satisfying the \"does the outcome change which\n83\tdownstream epics exist\" test. All Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts\n84\t(provider configuration, BFF code, benchmark report, provisioning logic). All three\n85\tbranch epics have `gate_failure_impact` with both `action` and a substantive\n86\t`fallback_approach`. No epic lists an Investigation in `dependencies` without `gated_by`\n87\t(the branch epics set it; no main-plan epic depends on E001). `gated_by` targets all\n88\tappear in the corresponding direct `dependencies` lists. E001 carries\n89\t`investigation_signals` and the Implementation epics carry `ai_signals` — type-correct\n90\tsignal fields.\n91\t\n92\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n93\tAll seven epics have type-appropriate signal fields in frontmatter and a matching\n94\t`-ai-signals.md` rationale file; rationale values match frontmatter values. E001's\n95\tinvestigation signals are well calibrated: `source_accessibility: 0` (the gating answer\n96\tis the in-progress RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery — no readable artifact holds it yet),\n97\t`human_judgment_required: -2` (the gating question is itself a sprint-planning\n98\tgo/no-go), `question_specificity: 1` (enumerable questions with pass/fail criteria).\n99\tImplementation signals check out against the strategy and the architecture context:\n100\tE002's favorable scores are corroborated by ogx-distribution.md (env-var-guarded\n101\tprovider activation; vector I/O via Milvus/PGVector/Qdrant; inline providers stripped\n102\tfrom the build) — verified present in `.context`; E003's `open_questions: 0` with a\n103\t\"partially resolved\" rationale (secret shape depends on the go/no-go) is honest;\n104\tBRANCH-A's `external_dependency: -1` (hard RHAISTRAT-7164 dependency) and BRANCH-B's\n105\t`open_questions: -1` (lifecycle-without-reconciliation-loop design unresolved, flagged\n106\tby Staff Engineer Input) are correct; E004's 0s for pattern/adapter/foundation (new\n107\tbenchmark harness) are justified. `architecture_claims` calibration verified against\n108\t`.context`: every +1 cites a context file that exists and corroborates the epic's\n109\tpremise (ogx-distribution.md, odh-dashboard.md, model-registry-operator.md,\n110\togx-k8s-operator.md, ai4rag.md); BRANCH-A's rationale correctly distinguishes what the\n111\tcontext file corroborates from what rests on Staff Engineer Input's own citations.\n112\tComputed totals/classifications not