{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a086a635bc35cbd4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E005\n3\ttitle: BFF-managed PostgreSQL provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If BFF-managed provisioning proves unworkable (lifecycle management\n16\t    without a reconciliation loop), fall back to requiring bring-your-own PostgreSQL\n17\t    with users configuring the OGXServer custom resource connection details.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# BFF-managed PostgreSQL provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tImplements backend-managed provisioning of the default vector store: the gen-ai\n39\tbackend-for-frontend provisions the PostgreSQL/pgvector instance directly —\n40\tcreating the Deployment, Service, persistent storage, and credentials secret\n41\twhen a playground with RAG is configured and no instance already exists in the\n42\tnamespace — mirroring how the backend currently provisions guardrails\n43\tinfrastructure. Because the backend is not an operator with a reconciliation\n44\tloop, lifecycle management (cleanup on playground deletion, pod-restart\n45\tresilience, credential rotation) receives explicit design attention. The design\n46\tis portable: when a platform-provided shared PostgreSQL becomes available in a\n47\tlater release, the backend consumes the shared connection string instead of\n48\tself-provisioning. This branch executes if the provisioning go/no-go decision\n49\tselects BFF-managed provisioning.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Implement idempotent provisioning logic in the gen-ai backend-for-frontend:\n54\t  create the PostgreSQL/pgvector Deployment, Service, persistent volume claim,\n55\t  and credentials secret in the playground namespace only when a playground\n56\t  with RAG is configured and no suitable instance exists.\n57\t- Implement cleanup of the provisioned resources on playground deletion.\n58\t- Design and implement handling for pod restarts and credential rotation\n59\t  without an operator reconciliation loop.\n60\t- Structure connection consumption for portability: consume a connection secret\n61\t  reference that can later point at a platform-provided shared PostgreSQL\n62\t  instead of a self-provisioned instance.\n63\t- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included) — no custom\n64\t  image build.\n65\t- Set resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator\n66\t  PostgreSQL reference values, adjusted per the benchmark findings.\n67\t- Validate end-to-end playground RAG workflows with the BFF-provisioned default\n68\t  vector store (with the pgvector provider integration and the\n69\t  backend-for-frontend provider wiring in place).\n70\t\n71\t## Acceptance Criteria\n72\t\n73\t- Configuring a playground with RAG in a namespace where no suitable PostgreSQL\n74\t  instance exists results in the backend-for-frontend creating the\n75\t  PostgreSQL/pgvector Deployment, Service, persistent storage, and credentials\n76\t  secret, with no manual user setup of external infrastructure.\n77\t- Deleting the playground cleans up the backend-provisioned PostgreSQL\n78\t  resources.\n79\t- Handling for pod restarts and credential rotation without a reconciliation\n80\t  loop is designed, documented, and implemented.\n81\t- The connection-consumption path is portable: the backend can consume a\n82\t  platform-provided shared connection string instead of self-provisioning when\n83\t  one becomes available.\n84\t- End-to-end Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function out-of-the-box with\n85\t  the BFF-provisioned default vector store, with no loss of current capability.\n86\t\n87\t## HLR Traceability\n88\t\n89\t- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning).\n90\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability).\n91\t- AC-4 (vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX\n92\t  instance).\n93\t- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping — per-namespace isolation).\n94\t- AC-6 (lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments).\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-831cbe92923c654c","agent_id":"abdd64eda1daf9810","session_id":"6460c734-9da5-4d64-9956-6c822c41e6b0","uuid":"c62b919c-2e70-4bec-b3d3-13392a057b88","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:28:12.585Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a086a635bc35cbd4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 round 2"}
