t | Protocol | Encryption | TLS Mode | Exposure |\n103\t|----|----|-----|----|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n104\t\n105\t### Egress\n106\t\n107\t| Destination | Port | Protocol | Encryption | Auth | Purpose |\n108\t|-----------|----|--------|----------|----|-------|\n109\t\n110\t## Security\n111\t\n112\t### RBAC - Cluster Roles\n113\t\n114\t| Role Name | API Group | Resources | Verbs |\n115\t|---------|---------|---------|-----|\n116\t\n117\t### RBAC - Role Bindings\n118\t\n119\t| Binding Name | Namespace | Role | Service Account |\n120\t|------------|---------|----|---------------|\n121\t\n122\t### Secrets\n123\t\n124\t| Secret Name | Type | Purpose | Provisioned By | Auto-Rotate |\n125\t|-----------|----|-------|--------------|-----------|\n126\t\n127\t### Authentication & Authorization\n128\t\n129\t| Endpoint | Methods | Auth Mechanism | Enforcement Point | Policy |\n130\t|--------|-------|--------------|-----------------|------|\n131\t| OGX API | All | OAuth2 bearer token (JWKS) | OGX server (built-in) | Owner-based resource isolation: read system resources; create for authenticated; read/update/delete for owners |\n132\t\n133\t### Security Evidence\n134\t\n135\t| Kind | Target | Detail | Signal Type |\n136\t|----|------|------|-----------|\n137\t\n138\t### FIPS Compliance\n139\t\n140\tThis is a Python application built on an AIPCC base image. FIPS compliance depends on the base image's OpenSSL configuration and the Python `cryptography` library's binding to the system OpenSSL.\n141\t\n142\t#### Application-Level Crypto\n143\t\n144\t| Aspect | Value | Source |\n145\t|--------|-------|--------|\n146\t| **Crypto libraries** | cryptography==50.0.0 (OpenSSL binding via cffi) | distribution/requirements-lock-konflux.txt:129 |\n147\t| **TLS configuration** | Per-provider `tls_verify` flags; defaults to `true` for vLLM providers; JWKS auth uses configurable `verify_tls` | distribution/config.yaml:31,265 |\n148\t| **Certificate handling** | System trust store (inherited from UBI base); configurable CA paths for Milvus (`ca_pem_path`, `client_pem_path`) and auth (`tls_cafile`) | distribution/config.yaml:89-91,268 |\n149\t| **Non-FIPS crypto risks** | No explicit FIPS opt-in detected; FIPS mode depends on base image OpenSSL configuration; `--insecure` flag passed to `ogx run` in entrypoint (controls application-level behavior, not TLS) | distribution/entrypoint.sh:79 |\n150\t\n151\t_The Python `cryptography` library binds to system OpenSSL via cffi. On a FIPS-enabled UBI base image, OpenSSL operates in FIPS mode and Python crypto operations use FIPS-validated algorithms. No explicit FIPS opt-in or non-FIPS algorithm usage was detected in the distribution configuration. The `--insecure` flag on `ogx run` is an OGX framework parameter controlling internal validation behavior, not a TLS or FIPS bypass._\n152\t## Data Flows\n153\t\n154\t### Flow 1: Inference Request\n155\t\n156\t| Step | Source | Destination | Port | Protocol | Encryption | Auth |\n157\t|------|--------|-------------|------|----------|------------|------|\n158\t| 1 | Client | OGX Server | 8321/TCP | HTTP | Platform-delegated | OAuth2 bearer token (when configured) |\n159\t| 2 | OGX Server | Inference Provider (vLLM / cloud) | Configurable | HTTP/HTTPS | TLS (configurable per provider) | API token / IAM / bearer token |\n160\t| 3 | OGX Server | PostgreSQL | 5432/TCP | PostgreSQL | Platform-delegated | Username/password |\n161\t\n162\t### Flow 2: RAG Query\n163\t\n164\t| Step | Source | Destination | Port | Protocol | Encryption | Auth |\n165\t|------|--------|-------------|------|----------|------------|------|\n166\t| 1 | Client | OGX Server | 8321/TCP | HTTP | Platform-delegated | OAuth2 bearer token (when configured) |\n167\t| 2 | OGX Server | Vector DB (Milvus / PGVector / Qdrant) | Configurable | HTTP/gRPC/SQL | Configurable (mTLS for Milvus) | Token / API key / password |\n168\t| 3 | OGX Server | Inference Provider | Configurable | HTTP/HTTPS | TLS | API t